hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"79","On Laylat al-Qadr. Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Khaldah narrated to us; I heard Abu al-Aliyah narrating that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying and said to him: When is Laylat al-Qadr? He said: Seek it in the first night and the last night, and in the odd nights."
